==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|arpeggiare||to play a [[harp]]|lang=it}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|music|lang=en}} The notes of a chord played individually instead of simultaneously, usually moving from lowest to highest.
#*{{quote-book|year=1956|author=[[w:Delano Ames|Delano Ames]]|title=Crime out of Mind|chapter=14|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5915292W|passage=He struck the opening chords of the passage; but this time Irene's voice was silent.  Victor stopped in the middle of an '''arpeggio'''.}}

